# fixedbugs, defect 571, lane b18-guard, 2026-10-10 (panel 205's R5).
#
# SYMPTOM: a struct marked `deprecated`, bound as a record the program never
# names in its own code: clang printed its warning at the record's field
# assertion and its per-type functions, the compiler's lines, at exit 0.
#
# FIX: `-Wdeprecated-declarations` is quiet on the compiler's own lines, from
# the groups' close and over each group constant's accessor and the
# per-type functions, and spoken over the program's own definitions
# (`emit/deprecation.hero`): the verdict is the one it was.

extern "fixedbugs-571-a-deprecated-record-bound-prints-no-clang-words.h"
    record OldPair tag old_pair
        a: i64
    function one() -> i64

function main()
    print(one())
